### Entry and home screens  [ADDED 2026-11-11 · D-107, D-108]

Sign-in, OTP, faster sign-in offer, returning unlock and Home share **one band** and **one screen standard** below it. Build the band once as a shared block; screens never restyle it. Spacing values below are **visible gaps** (§8.3) unless marked "box".

**The band (D-107)** — layout values, measured as boxes:

| Part | Value | Token |
|---|---|---|
| Band surface | Full-width light blue | `--tm-surface-brand-subtle` |
| Band padding | Top 16 from the safe area · sides 16 · bottom 32 | `--tm-space-lg` · `--tm-space-page` · `--tm-space-2xl` |
| Logo lockup | 166 wide, left (§8.13). The header row is the logo's height; nothing in it adds height. | `--tm-logo-lockup-width` |
| Logo → title | **16** (L6) | `--tm-space-lg` |
| Title | L1 32/40 semibold, primary, one line, balanced (L8) | `.tm-text-title-lg`, `--tm-content-primary` |
| Title → subtitle | 8 | `--tm-space-sm` |
| Subtitle | L3 14/20, secondary, one line; nothing inside it may grow its 20 line box | `.tm-text-body-md`, `--tm-content-secondary` |
| Subtitle → panel | 32 | `--tm-space-2xl` |
| Panel | Top corners 24, top padding 32, sides 16, white | `--tm-radius-2xl` · `--tm-space-2xl` · `--tm-space-page` · `--tm-surface-primary` |

- **Result:** the panel top lands at 173 on every screen at 390 × 844 and 360 × 640. It follows from the content flow; never hard-code it.
- **Copy check:** every fixed title and subtitle fits one line at 360 wide (≤ 328 px). Never `nowrap` or clip: enlarged text and long content wrap (WCAG 1.4.4).
- **Allowed variants, and no others:**
  1. **Home header actions** (bell, help, profile): 48 targets, last glyph 16 from the edge (B-07). They never add height.
  2. **A title carrying a name** ("Hello, Dr. {name}") may wrap to two balanced lines. The band grows by one line. Never truncate or shrink the name.
  3. **OTP subtitle:** the number in primary medium and "Change" as an inline link (`.tm-link`, §9.1). The link's 48 hit area adds no height.
  4. **State and device wording** may change. The spacing doesn't.
- **Notices, busy buttons and keyboards stay in the panel.** The band never changes with state.

**Below the band — the screen standard (D-108; screens audit §1 with visible values):**

| Part | Spec | Token / source |
|---|---|---|
| Panel | Content starts **32** below the panel top. Side margins 16. | `--tm-space-2xl`, `--tm-space-page` |
| Group label | 16/24 semibold, **8** to its control. An optional helper (14/20 grey) sits right-aligned on the same line. | `--tm-space-sm` |
| Field | Label 14/20 semibold → **8** → control → **8** → helper or error, 14/20, one slot (L4, L7). Field + helper → **32** → the next thing (sign-in: → Send OTP). | `.tm-field`, `--tm-space-sm`, `--tm-space-2xl` |
| Field message (no bar) | "Couldn't send the OTP." and similar: **16** under the field, **32** above the next thing (sign-in: Send OTP). | `.tm-notice`, `--tm-space-lg`, `--tm-space-2xl` |
| OTP code | 56 boxes 8 apart (L1). Boxes (+ the reserved message line) → **32** → "Didn't receive it? Resend" → **32** → legal line → **8** → Verify. Locked / expired-and-limited: boxes → **16** → notice → **32** → Verify. | D-44, D-108 |
| Whole-screen notice | At the top of its content, or under the thing it blocks (locked, unavailable), then **32** to the next thing. | §9.5 |
| Inline primary (typing screens) | **32** below the group above it. **8** under a legal line that describes it. Kept visible above the keyboard by scrolling, 16 clear (§8.9). | §8.4 |
| Pinned bar | Padding 16 + safe area. Buttons 56/18, primary → quiet, 8 apart (box). Bar notice: full-width band, centred, 16 above its button. Caption line ("Available until 7:45 PM"): L3 centred, 8 above its button. The content scrolls, with ≥ 16 clear at the end. | `.tm-actionbar`, §9.5 |
| Hero tile | 64 tile, radius lg, brand-subtle, 32 glyph, centred, at panel top + 32. Then **32** to the content under it (offer: → points). Unlock: tile → **16** → caption. | `--tm-icon-tile-size` |
| Points | Neutral 24 icon · 12 · title 16/24 **semibold** · line 14/20 grey; title → line 8; **16** between points. | §8.11 |
| Card rows | One `tm-card`. Rows: padding 16, a hairline between rows. Grey icon · label 16/24 regular · value L9. Cards stacked 16 apart. | `.tm-card`, L9 |
| Links | Brand colour. Semibold when the link is the line's action (Change, Resend code, Sign up), as `.tm-link` with a 48 hit area that adds no height. Regular inside legal text (`.tm-link--in-sentence`). Visible focus. | §8.6, §9.1 |
| Fine print | L4 12/16 only for the OTP legal consent. Nothing else the doctor reads or taps is under 14. | §8.1 |
| Sheet | Header: title 20/28 + ✕ 48, **subtitle 8 under the title inside the header** (D-109). Header → content 16; content → actions 24; actions 8 apart; 24 + safe area at the bottom. A result notice sits inside the pinned actions, 16 above its button. | §9.4 |
| Duration picker | One block on setup and in the add-time sheet. "Quick picks" (6 chips, 3 columns, 8 / 8) → **32** → "Custom" → column heads 4 (box) → wheel of 3 × 48 rows. No range text (D-106). | D-40, D-106 |
| Type | Four levels + L9. One weight per role: 16/24 emphasis is always semibold (600); medium is not used below the band. | §8.1 |
| Words | **OTP** for the SMS code outside the OTP screen; **code** only on the OTP screen. **Faster sign-in** for the feature. **Availability** for the window, **time** for its length, **case** for the work, **get** for new cases (D-109). | — |

**Check:** `design-system/scripts/check-visible-gaps.mjs` (§8.3) runs on every in-scope screen and state at 390 × 844 and 360 × 640. A project's config maps its own classes onto the roles above (label, field, helper, notice, legal, link line, tile, caption, group label).
### 9.4 Bottom sheets — one template
| Part | Rule |
|---|---|
| Background | Page dimmed behind the sheet (`.tm-overlay`). |
| Top | Rounded top corners; **no drag handle** (the ✕ is always there). |
| Header | Title 20/28 semibold, left · ✕ right (48px target, glyph on the 16 margin — the same as the compact task header, B-07) · **no divider**. Optional subtitle (L3) **8 under the title, inside the header** (D-109, 2026-11-11): wrap title and subtitle in `.tm-sheet__heading`. The title line stays centred on the ✕. |
| Spacing | 16px side margins (`--tm-space-page`, same as screens) · 16px header → content · 24px + safe area at the bottom. |
| Content | Fields, chips, or **option rows** (one shared style for reason lists: title + one-line description, full width, 48px+; tapping applies). Labels inside a sheet ("Select reason", "Date", "Time") use `.tm-sheet__label` — one style, 8 above the field (B-14, 2026-11-02). |
| Actions | §9.1 order and size (56px, full width). **Pinned (Round 6, 2026-11-02):** the actions are the sheet's last part and stay on screen when the content is taller than the space — the content scrolls between the pinned header and the pinned actions. The hairline and soft upward shadow show only while content scrolls under them (`design-system/src/sheet-scroll.js` sets `.is-stuck`; screens with sheets load it). Sheet buttons stay fully visible and tappable at 390×844 and 360×640. Reason lists need no button. **Confirmation sheet** ("Leave this case?", "Discard changes?"): the action the sheet asks about on top — red outline if it can't easily be undone, primary otherwise — and the "stay" option as quiet text below. A sheet offering two real actions (e.g. Retry call / Mark as unavailable) is a choice, not a confirmation (D-54). |
| Closing | ✕, tap outside or swipe down = cancel — **except while an action is in progress**. Unsaved input asks before closing. |
| Size | Up to 85% of the screen height; the content scrolls, header and actions stay pinned. Max width 640px on desktop. |
| Over the bar | **A sheet always covers the pinned action bar of the screen behind it (Round 6, 2026-11-02).** The scrim and the sheet sit above the bar in every state: no part of the bar shows or takes a tap while a sheet is open. |
- **Quiet text for "stay" (D-81 F11):** the option that keeps things as they are ("Stay signed in", "Keep available") is quiet text (`tm-btn--quiet`), never a secondary button.

### 9.5 Feedback
| Surface | Rule |
|---|---|
| **Field error** | Under the field (L4, L7). |
// The one band (D-107, design-system/RULES.md "Entry and home screens"): sign-in, OTP, faster sign-in offer, returning unlock and
// Home build it here and never restyle it. Logo 16 from the top (safe area) · logo → title 16 · title L1 · title → subtitle 8 ·
// subtitle L3 one 20 line · subtitle → panel 32. The panel (white, radius 24, top padding 32) is `.entry-panel`; with this band
// its top lands at 173 on every screen. Allowed variants: Home header actions (`actions`), a title carrying a name may wrap
// (it wraps naturally), the OTP subtitle's number + `.tm-link` Change (`subtitle` as nodes). Styles: band.css.
import { h } from "../core/dom.js";
import { MSG } from "../core/msg.js";

export function band({ title, titleId, subtitle, actions = null, tag = "header" }) {
  return h(tag, { class: "entry-band band" },
    h("div", { class: "entry-band__row" },
      h("img", { class: "entry-band__logo login-logo", src: "brand/truemeds-for-doctors.svg", alt: MSG("signin.logoAlt") }),
      actions ? h("div", { class: "entry-band__actions" }, actions) : null),
    h("h1", { class: "entry-band__title", id: titleId, text: title }),
    h("p", { class: "entry-band__sub sub" }, subtitle));
}
/* The one band (D-107) and the white panel under it — shared by sign-in, OTP, faster sign-in offer, returning unlock and Home.
   Spec: design-system/RULES.md "Entry and home screens". Screens never restyle these classes. Tokens only. */
.entry-band { flex: none; padding: var(--tm-space-lg) var(--tm-space-page) var(--tm-space-2xl); background: var(--tm-surface-brand-subtle); color: var(--tm-content-primary); }
/* Header row: the logo's height; nothing in it adds height (Home actions overhang, B-07). */
.entry-band__row { display: flex; align-items: flex-start; justify-content: space-between; }
.entry-band__logo { display: block; width: var(--tm-logo-lockup-width); height: auto; margin: 0; }   /* §8.13: 166 wide, height from the artwork */
.entry-band__actions { display: flex; align-self: center; gap: var(--tm-space-xs);
  margin: calc((var(--tm-icon-size-md) - var(--tm-target-min)) / 2) calc((var(--tm-icon-size-md) - var(--tm-target-min)) / 2) calc((var(--tm-icon-size-md) - var(--tm-target-min)) / 2) 0; }
/* L6 (D-107): logo → title 16 · title L1 32/40, balanced (L8); a title carrying a name may wrap to two lines (variant 2). */
.entry-band__title { margin: var(--tm-space-lg) 0 0; font-size: var(--tm-font-size-title-lg); line-height: var(--tm-font-lineheight-2xl); font-weight: var(--tm-font-weight-semibold); color: var(--tm-content-primary); text-wrap: balance; }
/* Title → subtitle 8 · subtitle L3 14/20, one 20 line box: nothing inside may grow it (a .tm-link's 48 hit area adds no height). */
.entry-band__sub { margin: var(--tm-space-sm) 0 0; font-size: var(--tm-font-size-body-md); line-height: var(--tm-font-lineheight-sm); color: var(--tm-content-secondary); }
.entry-band__sub b { color: var(--tm-content-primary); font-weight: var(--tm-font-weight-medium, 500); }   /* OTP number (variant 3) */
/* The panel: radius 24 on top, top padding 32, sides 16, white. Content starts 32 below its top (D-108). */
.entry-panel { flex: 1; min-height: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; box-sizing: border-box; background: var(--tm-surface-primary);
  border-radius: var(--tm-radius-2xl) var(--tm-radius-2xl) 0 0; padding: var(--tm-space-2xl) var(--tm-space-page) var(--tm-space-xl); }
// Home, availability and Profile (plan v3.2 step 2). Markup and classes lifted from ui-screens/home/home-reference.js
// (header, band, panel, wheel picker, action bar footer, add / end sheets, Profile page, Log out sheet); styles in home.css.
// Behaviour: app-logic §3 (pull model, availability window, add / end, Prescriptions today, Profile, Log out) and the Home rows
// of docs/feedback-state-map.md. Every word through MSG(). A state opened directly (?s=home_<state>) shows the picture's
// moment, then behaves live (requests resolve, the clock runs) — except capture, which stays on the picture's moment.
import { MSG } from "../core/msg.js";
import { push, replace, reset as resetNav, back as navBack, depth, setScreenBack, saveCurrent } from "../core/nav.js";
import { store } from "../core/store.js";
import { clock } from "../core/clock.js";
import { h } from "../core/dom.js";
import { value } from "../core/settings.js";
import { storageFor } from "../core/storage.js";
import { promptAnswer, deviceOf } from "../core/unlock.js";
import { fasterState, setEnabled } from "../core/faster-signin.js";
import { work, saveWork, resetWork, availability, setAvailability, addTime, endAvailability, startRequest, clearRequest, openCase } from "../core/session.js";
import { SAMPLE_DOCTOR } from "../data/doctor.js";
import { PICTURE_NUMBER } from "../data/test-numbers.js";
import { icon, paint as paintIcons, btn, busyBtn, notice, statusLine, actionBar, sheet, toast, focusSheet } from "./parts.js";
import { newLife } from "./entry-ctx.js";
import { wheelColumn, syncWheels, commitWheels } from "./wheel.js";
import { band } from "./band.js";
import { parts } from "../core/dom.js";

const MIN = 60 * 1000;
// Picture moments (home-reference.js STATES). left: minutes remaining; rx: Prescriptions today; bar: the bar result notice.
const FIXTURES = {
  "setup-wheel": { setup: true, rx: 0 },
  setting: { setup: true, rx: 0, busy: "setting" },
  "setup-failed": { setup: true, rx: 0, bar: "setup-failed" },
  active: { left: 30 },
  requesting: { left: 30, request: true, busy: "requesting" },
  "no-cases": { left: 30, bar: "no-cases" },
  "request-failed": { left: 30, bar: "request-failed" },
  offline: { left: 30, offline: true },
  "near-expiry": { left: 5 },
  "add-wheel": { left: 5, sheet: "add" },
  adding: { left: 5, sheet: "add", busy: "adding" },
  "add-failed": { left: 5, sheet: "add", addFailed: true },
  added: { left: 35, toast: true },
  "end-confirmation": { left: 30, sheet: "end" },
  "stop-pending": { left: 30, request: true, stopping: true },
  "expired-pending": { left: 0, request: true },
  "idle-expired": { setup: true, ended: "idle" },
  "manually-ended": { setup: true, ended: "manual" },
  "unknown-result": { left: 30, request: true, unknown: true },
  profile: { left: 30, page: "profile" },
  "profile-case-open": { left: 30, page: "profile", caseOpen: true },
  "logout-confirm": { left: 30, page: "profile", sheet: "logout" },
};
export const STATES = Object.keys(FIXTURES).map((k) => `home_${k}`);
const PRESETS = [15, 30, 45, 60, 120, 180];
const presetLabel = (n) => n < 60 ? MSG("home.presetMinutes", { n }) : n === 60 ? MSG("home.presetHour") : MSG("home.presetHours", { n: n / 60 });
// "Add 9 h 45 min": minutes under an hour, hours and minutes from 60 min up (D-106).
export const durationLabel = (n) => n < 60 ? MSG("home.durMinutes", { m: n }) : n % 60 ? MSG("home.durHoursMinutes", { h: Math.floor(n / 60), m: n % 60 }) : MSG("home.durHours", { h: n / 60 });
// "7:45 PM": the end of the window on the setup caption ("Available until {time}").
const clockTime = (t) => new Date(t).toLocaleTimeString("en-US", { hour: "numeric", minute: "2-digit" });
// The 10-hour cap (D-106) and the 15-minute minimum and step, in minutes. The wheel is in real minutes in every mode.
const CAP = value("availabilityMaximum", "review") / MIN, MIN_LEN = value("availabilityMinimum", "review") / MIN, STEP = value("availabilityStep", "review") / MIN;
// Wheel values for a top limit in minutes: hours 0 … top; at 0 h the minutes start at 15; at the top hour they stop at the limit.
const hoursFor = (max) => Array.from({ length: Math.floor(max / 60) + 1 }, (_, n) => n);
const minutesFor = (hh, max) => [0, 15, 30, 45].filter((m) => (hh > 0 || m >= MIN_LEN) && hh * 60 + m <= max);
// Snaps a wanted length onto the wheel: at least 15 min, at most the limit, on the 15-minute step.
const clampLen = (n, max) => Math.max(MIN_LEN, Math.min(Math.floor(max / STEP) * STEP, n));
// Timer: m:ss below an hour, h:mm:ss from one hour up (D-53).
export function formatLeft(ms) {
  const s = Math.max(0, Math.ceil(ms / 1000)), hh = Math.floor(s / 3600), mm = Math.floor((s % 3600) / 60), ss = s % 60;
  const p = (n) => String(n).padStart(2, "0");
  return hh ? `${hh}:${p(mm)}:${p(ss)}` : `${mm}:${p(ss)}`;
}

// Applies a picture moment to the session (fixtures are where a jump or ?s= starts; the session then plays on from there).
function applyFixture(fx, mode) {
  const now = clock.now();
  const rx = fx.rx ?? 3;
  const patch = { rxToday: rx, ended: fx.ended || null, stopping: !!fx.stopping, request: fx.request ? { at: now } : null, openCase: null };
  patch.avail = fx.setup ? null : { endsAt: now + fx.left * MIN };
  resetWork(patch);
  if (fx.caseOpen) openCase(store.get().scenario || "cat4", "normal");
}

export function render(host, id, { mode, params = {} }) {
  const key = id.replace(/^home_/, "");
  const fx = FIXTURES[key];
  if (!fx) return null;
  const life = newLife(host, mode);
  const live = !!params.live;
  const capture = mode === "capture";
  if (!live && !params.saved) applyFixture(fx, mode);
  // An open case comes first: Home (opened live) goes straight back into it (D-48, app-logic §4 "reopening goes back into the case").
  if (live && work().openCase && !fx.page) { queueMicrotask(() => replace(null, { s: "t01-ready", live: true })); return { journey: "caseView" }; }

  const story = () => store.get().story || {};
  const v = (k) => value(k, mode);
  const ui = {
    page: fx.page || "home",
    sheet: live ? null : fx.sheet || null,
    busy: live ? (work().request ? "requesting" : null) : fx.busy || null,
    bar: live ? null : fx.bar || null,
    unknown: !live && !!fx.unknown,
    offlineFx: !live && !!fx.offline,
    addFailed: !live && !!fx.addFailed,
    duration: 30, addDuration: 30,
    toastUntil: !live && fx.toast ? (capture ? Number.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER : Date.now() + v("toastDuration")) : 0,
    profileError: null, fasterBusy: false,
    ...(params.saved || {}),
  };
  const offline = () => ui.offlineFx || store.get().offline === "yes";

  const root = h("div", { class: "home-screen tm" });
  host.replaceChildren(root);

  // ---------- pieces ----------
  // A real swipe wheel per column (F-04, D-40): wheel.js. Busy (Setting… / Adding…) blocks it.
  function wheel(name, values, current, col) {
