ui-screens/app-logic.md:43:- 4 digits, keyboard opens on load and stays open while verifying. No auto-verify: the doctor taps **Verify & sign in**.
ui-screens/app-logic.md:51:- Expired code: Resend is available at once; the expired code can't be verified.
ui-screens/app-logic.md:54:- **SMS auto-fill (hand-off note, screens audit 2026-11-11):** the code field is a one-time-code field (`autocomplete="one-time-code"` in the prototype). On the phone use Android SMS User Consent (or the SMS Retriever API) and iOS `textContentType="oneTimeCode"`; the filled code still waits for **Verify & sign in** (no auto-verify). Check it on a real device.
ui-screens/app-logic.md:58:- Offered on its own screen after an OTP sign-in on a phone that supports it, while faster sign-in is off: after the first sign-in, then again at each later OTP sign-in until it is turned on, at most 3 times (setting `fasterOfferMax`, D-104; "not available" counts as shown). The footer is the action bar (Round 4, item 1); the content above it scrolls. Subtitle on one line: "Use your screen lock instead of an OTP." (A-06). **Turn on** → phone prompt → Home. **Cancelled** prompt → back to the offer, no message. **Failed** → stays on the offer; "Couldn't turn on faster sign-in." sits in the bar above Try again (A-19) · Try again · Not now (D-61, D-65). **Offline** → "You're offline. Check your connection." (D-66). **Unavailable** (the phone answers "unavailable" at Turn on) → stays on the offer, unchanged (title, subtitle, tile and the three points): the amber warning notice "Faster sign-in isn't available on this phone right now." sits in the bar (same slot as Offline and "Couldn't turn on", A-19), the primary reads **Continue** → Home and Not now is hidden; not enabled, recorded as offered, can be turned on later in Profile (D-93, state `offer_unavailable`). **Not now** → Home; offered again at the next OTP sign-in, up to `fasterOfferMax` times in total (D-104); can be turned on or off in Profile (D-69).
ui-screens/app-logic.md:60:- Returning unlock: two buttons (D-105), **Unlock** (primary) · **Use OTP instead** (quiet); no "Switch account". **The phone's prompt opens by itself once when the app opens on this screen (D-109 §3, amends D-38 / D-105)**; cancelling shows the screen as it is, with no new prompt; **Unlock** stays for a retry. The automatic prompt counts as a try: 3 failed tries `[MOCK]` → the same as Use OTP instead. A picture or a jump to an unlock state never prompts. Tile → 16 → "Ready when you are" (D-108); a greeting with a long name may wrap to two lines (D-107 variant 2). **Use OTP instead** opens **Sign-in with the remembered number filled in** (cursor at the end, Send OTP ready); no SMS is sent until the doctor taps Send OTP. To change account, the doctor edits the number there. This Sign-in follows the normal Sign-in rules: no Back; the phone's back gesture leaves the app (D-101); reopening the app shows unlock again. The footer is the action bar (Round 4, item 1); the content above it scrolls. If unavailable: "Faster sign-in isn't available on this phone right now." is a standing state, so the neutral notice stays at the top of the panel; **Use OTP instead** is the main button in the bar (A-19) and opens the same prefilled Sign-in.
ui-screens/app-logic.md:74:- **10 hours in total (D-106, replaces D-36 "no maximum"):** the setup wheel goes 0–10 h (at 10 h minutes 0 only; at 0 h 15 / 30 / 45). Setting `availabilityMaximum`.
ui-screens/app-logic.md:75:- **Available (D-106, D-107):** title "You can take cases" · subtitle "Request a case now, or whenever you’re ready." · one card (as on the case page) with two rows of one anatomy (grey icon · 16/24 regular label · L9 value): **Time remaining** with **+ Add time always shown** (compact secondary, on the value line; greyed offline) and **Prescriptions written today**, which opens Profile (chevron; Back returns to Home). Replaces A-09 ("Add time near expiry only") and A-10 (labels 14 grey).
ui-screens/app-logic.md:76:- **Time remaining:** h:mm:ss from one hour up (1:00:00), m:ss below (9:42). Shows 0:00 when it ran out with a request still open (D-53; no Add time then, the window has ended). Ending availability (stop-pending) has no time row (D-47).
ui-screens/app-logic.md:79:- **Add time (D-106):** always shown while available (greyed offline, and greyed when less than 15 minutes fit under the 10-hour total — `[MOCK ASSUMPTION]`, D-106 is silent). Sheet title "Add time", subtitle "Choose how much time to add." (8 under the title, inside the header, D-109); the same Quick picks / Custom picker; the wheel tops out at what is left of the 10 hours (rounded down to 15 minutes), hint "Up to 10 hours in total" on the Custom line; quick picks above that are greyed. Button "Add 30 min", "Add 1 h", "Add 9 h 45 min" (hours and minutes from 60 min up). "Time added" toast. The error ("Couldn’t add time.") sits **in the pinned actions, 16 above Add**, so it shows on arrival at 360 × 640.
ui-screens/app-logic.md:88:- **Faster sign-in toggle (D-70):** turning it **off** just switches it off (no prompt; OTP from the next sign-in). Turning it **on** opens the phone's prompt, as on the offer screen; if that fails, the toggle stays off and the page shows "Couldn't turn on faster sign-in."; cancelling leaves it off with no message. Hidden if the phone has no screen lock at all (D-64).
ui-screens/app-logic.md:103:| Transfer ready (`call.transfer-ready` 12) | Script stays (call still live) | **Confirm & transfer** · Skip HA (full width, under it; no Callback, CW-A1) — shown only once the backend confirms gate time since the patient answered and the call is live (D-58 pt 14) | Blocked |
ui-screens/app-logic.md:112:**Leaving a case:** the back-blocked toast breaks between its two sentences (B-21). An **attempted call** = leg 2 answered (the patient picked up) (D-58). Once a call is attempted, leaving is blocked until the case is closed (callback, unavailable, confirm). Before that, header **Back** opens the "Leave this case?" sheet — **Release case** (the case returns to the queue) or **Stay** (D-58 point 20, OQ-024; label D-84 CA-22; on Ready and states 3 and 4 only). Header Back is on 1, 3 and 4 only, while the patient has never been reached. It is hidden from the **Call patient** / **Call again** tap, incl. Calling 7a, the 7b question, Transfer, and the callback sheets, and never returns once the patient answered, also on a later 3 / 4 (D-80 pt 1, D-81 F21). Behind the leave sheet, Releasing… and Release failed the screen is **Ready** (D-81 F22). The backend refuses Release once our call request is accepted, unless the result is 3 or 4 (D-80). Release returns the doctor to Home (CW-A5). If the patient answered just before the tap, the backend refuses the release and the doctor stays on the case (`a-release-failed`, "Couldn't release this case. You're still on it."). The unassign action itself is a backend dependency (OQ-024). Help stays available at every stage and is the way to reach Doctor Ops when something keeps failing. App closed or phone off mid-case → reopening goes straight back into the case `[OPEN OQ-025, backend]`.
ui-screens/app-logic.md:114:**End-of-call script** (D-58 points 18, 21, 24 — copy keys in `messages.json`). Shown from the tap on Call while a call may be live; **hidden once the call has ended** (no one to read it to), except after a failed transfer (15) and B3, where the doctor is still on the line:
ui-screens/app-logic.md:155:| 7f | `call.submitted` | Waiting for the call record | Confirm in 7d (or Confirm & forward on the Pilot route) | Grey card "Waiting for the call record · Your prescription is saved. We'll confirm it once the record arrives." (D-68); On the Cat4 route it becomes "Prescription confirmed" (10a) when the record arrives; on the Pilot route (Confirm & forward on 7d) it becomes **10b Forwarded to Health Advisor** (D-89, Q-A). **Under the gate, the patient never answered, or no record after a wait time (setting)** → not confirmed, back through hold and retry; no Ops review queue (CW-D3, CW-D4) · Request next case · Back to Home | `s7f-submitted` |
ui-screens/app-logic.md:159:| 9 | `call.patient-unavailable` | Patient unavailable (automatic) | Leg 2 failed | Grey card · Request next case · Back to Home | `t09-patient-unavailable` |
ui-screens/app-logic.md:174:Retired: `b-missed-call`, `b-didnt-connect` (sheets) — replaced by the automatic close and the notices. `a-leave-sheet` / `s7e-leave-sheet` is the approved Release sheet (D-58 point 20). The old state name **hold** for "didn't connect" is retired (old Flag 4).
ui-screens/app-logic.md:178:**Dependency (Engineering):** the app gets call status by polling the backend (D-58 pt 19). Hiding Back once the patient answers and the transfer count both need **live** leg events from the partner during the call (leg 1 answered, leg 2 answered / Ozonetel `customerAnswered`), not only the result at the end (OQ-030).
ui-screens/app-logic.md:197:**7d follows the route (CW-D2, D-83):** Cat4 / HA skipped → **Confirm prescription**; Pilot with an HA call → **Confirm & forward** (the transfer is no longer possible once the call has ended). Secondaries: **Callback + Unavailable**; no Skip HA on 7d. **Skip HA** on 8b, 12 and 16 sits full width under the main button (D-83, K1).
ui-screens/app-logic.md:199:- **Skip HA** only after the gate, for **both Pilot types** (Value and Non-Value Meds) whenever an HA call follows the doctor call and it isn't already skipped — no other conditions (D-59). Opens the reason sheet: Patient declined HA call · Clinically not required · Repeat patient, familiar with the medicines — Counselled in an earlier order (D-70 item 3; title and sub-line). Choosing a reason applies it at once. On a call with a result the final button becomes **Confirm prescription**; during a live transfer call the case then waits for the call result (state 17, D-58 point 14). Skip HA is also offered after a missed transfer (state 16, D-58 point 24).
ui-screens/app-logic.md:220:- **By the doctor** only in 7d (result not received); state 6 has no Unavailable (D-58 pt 23). **Unavailable** opens the reason sheet "Mark patient unavailable" (D-75): Didn't answer · Not reachable · Wrong number. Choosing a reason closes the case at once (it is the confirmation); × backs out with no change. **The reason is saved with the case** for Ops monitoring (D-73).
ui-screens/app-logic.md:260:- **✕ with changes** → "Discard changes?" sheet: **Discard** (red outline) on top, Keep editing below (D-54). No changes → closes at once.
ui-screens/app-logic.md:261:- **Disable** → sheet "Disable {name}" with reasons: Can’t prescribe remotely · Contraindicated for patient · Duplicate medication · Patient declined · Wrong strength. Choosing a reason disables it at once (status Disabled). A disabled medicine is **removed from the order**; the order ships without it. If no medicine is left, the order is cancelled later (ops/backend). No extra warning for the last medicine — the reason sheet is the friction (D-59).
ui-screens/app-logic.md:290:- **Profile earnings (D-81 F10):** **₹20 per confirmed prescription** (Apurva, 2026-11-02), so 3 prescriptions today show Earned ₹60.00 · Incentive ₹0.00 (0 while setting availability). The app shows what the backend sends; earnings count once a case is confirmed (D-73). Incentive rules are not defined yet (₹0.00 in the prototype).
ui-screens/app-logic.md:325:OQ-017 OTP lock and window lengths · OQ-019 no-cases auto re-check · OQ-024 release backend · OQ-025 restoring an open case · timer behaviour on hold (OQ-001) · doctor volume figures (OQ-029).
docs/prd/PRD.md:15:Truemeds doctors are freelance doctors who call patients who ordered prescription medicines, review each medicine and issue the prescription. Today they do this on a portal page that also carries pricing, substitutes, billing and cross-selling, and the call itself happens outside the page with no status inside it. The doctor app gives the doctor one job per screen: say when they're available, request a case, call the patient, prescribe or disable each medicine, and close the case the one right way for its case type. The system, not the doctor, decides which final button appears, and a prescription only counts once the call is proven to be a real consultation. Open items are mainly with Engineering (live call events, call-record timing, releasing and restoring cases) and a few product calls, listed in §10.
docs/prd/PRD.md:65:- Input that can still become right shows no error while typing; input that can never be right (a first digit that no Indian mobile number has) is flagged at once. The doctor isn't told off for typing.
docs/prd/PRD.md:110:**What the doctor can do:** type the 4-digit code; tap Verify & sign in; tap Change to fix the number; tap Resend code once the wait is over.
docs/prd/PRD.md:116:- An expired code can't be verified; Resend is available at once.
docs/prd/PRD.md:139:- The phone's own prompt makes sense right after a deliberate Turn on.
docs/prd/PRD.md:147:**What the doctor can do:** Turn on faster sign-in (opens the phone's prompt, then Home); Not now (goes to Home; asked again at the next OTP sign-in).
docs/prd/PRD.md:170:- The phone's fingerprint / Face ID / screen-lock prompt opens by itself when the app opens, as banking and payment apps do, which saves a tap every time.
docs/prd/PRD.md:182:- The phone's prompt opens by itself once when the app opens here. Cancelling it leaves the screen as it is, with no new prompt; Unlock stays for a retry. The automatic prompt counts as a try.
docs/prd/PRD.md:190:- Prompt cancelled (on arrival or after Unlock) → back on the screen, no message, no new prompt.
docs/prd/PRD.md:191:- Phone asks to retry → the phone's own retry prompt.
docs/prd/PRD.md:209:**What the doctor can do:** set how long they're available ("Start taking cases": Quick picks 15, 30 and 45 minutes, 1, 2 and 3 hours, or Custom, a wheel in 15-minute steps, with "Available until {time}" above Set availability); Request a case ("You can take cases"); Add time at any point while available; tap Prescriptions written today to open Profile; End availability; open Profile, Help and notifications.
docs/prd/PRD.md:212:- Availability has a minimum and a **maximum in total**, set plus added time (§7), any start time. Add time tops out at what is left of the maximum, and the sheet says so; the button names the time it adds in hours and minutes.
docs/prd/PRD.md:213:- Home shows one card: time remaining, with Add time always on its line (greyed offline), and prescriptions written today (a count only, no earnings), which opens Profile. A case counts once its prescription is confirmed. After availability ends, the count shows as one row above the picker when it is above 0.
docs/prd/PRD.md:229:- Ending soon → "Availability ends soon. You can still request a case." (Add time is always there).
docs/prd/PRD.md:257:- The backend refuses a release once the partner has accepted our call request for the case, unless the call didn't go through or the doctor didn't answer.
docs/prd/PRD.md:268:- Phone back once a call has started → toast "Finish this case first." "Then you can go back to Home."
docs/prd/PRD.md:273:**Job to be done:** talk to the patient and confirm the prescription once the call counts.
docs/prd/PRD.md:304:- From the tap on Call patient, while a call may be live, an end-of-call script for the patient shows on the case page. It hides once the call has ended.
docs/prd/PRD.md:307:**What the doctor can do:** Call patient; Call again when the call didn't go through, the doctor missed it or it was too short; answer "Are you still on the call?"; Confirm prescription once the call is valid; Callback when the call was too short or no result came; Patient unavailable when no result came (§5.9).
docs/prd/PRD.md:391:- Closing with unsaved changes asks "Discard changes?"; closing without changes closes at once.
docs/prd/PRD.md:401:| Capsule | capsule | 0 · 1 · 2 | 1 · 2 | — | `2 capsules once a week · 6 months` |
docs/prd/PRD.md:405:| Injection | units | 0 · 1 · 2 · 3 | 1 · 2 · 3 | any amount in units | `1 dose once a month · 3 months` |
docs/prd/PRD.md:465:| Maximum availability, in total (set + added time) | 10 hours | Product |
docs/prd/PRD.md:507:**Decided** (each stated once, in its section):
docs/prd/PRD.md:522:- Live events during the call from each partner: doctor's leg answered, patient's leg answered; polling interval; maximum call length; result wait time; how a failed Health Advisor transfer leg is reported. (OQ-030) [Engineering]
docs/prd/PRD.md:530:- The release action in the backend: refusing a release once our call request is accepted, and returning the case to the queue at once. (OQ-024) [Engineering]
docs/prd/PRD.md:564:| **Primary:** doctor-handled orders that end confirmed | orders ending in any of the four confirmed endings with a proven call ÷ orders a doctor opened (each order counted once, even if released to another doctor) | backend case outcomes | `[NEED (Doctor Ops)]` |
docs/prd/PRD.md:574:**Tracking rule:** the four endings (Cat4 confirmed, Pilot with HA skipped confirmed, transferred, forwarded) are separate outcomes and can never be worked out from the button text, because two of them share the label Confirm prescription. Renaming a button never renames an event. Release, Callback, Patient unavailable (automatic or by the doctor, with reason) and Skip HA (with reason) are tracked too. Event names are Engineering's choice. Calls are counted in Truemeds' funnel terms: a call is *attempted* when the patient's leg is *connected*.
docs/prd/PRD.md:580:- Pilot, Health Advisor reserved: the live call shows **Confirm & transfer** (with Skip HA) once the call is valid; the patient is handed over on the same call. If the transfer fails, the case goes as a forward.
