handoff/DECIDED.md:349:- **No raw values.** No hex codes, no `rgb`, no typed numbers for colour, spacing, radius, shadow, **sizes, border widths, timing, layering (z-index) or opacity** in component or project code (D-99). If a value isn't a token, it isn't allowed. Use a token by meaning, not by value (a 20px text line is `--tm-font-lineheight-sm`, not an icon size). Allowed exceptions carry a same-line `/* raw-ok: <reason> */` marker: geometry (`50%` centring, `100%`, `100vh`, `rotate(360deg)`, `line-height: 1`), optical nudges of 1–3px, the 31ch text measure, the hidden OTP input's 16px (stops iPhone zoom), reduced-motion `0.01ms`, `@media` widths, and prototype-only drawings (the drawn keyboard). Not scanned:,, the mock Rx paper, reference files and the `[DEPRECATED]` legacy `.tm-otp` block. — *Source: Design rules 2.1*
